```

---

### 2.3 Mimir Repo — All Concrete `storage.Querier` Implementors

#### `pkg/storage/lazyquery/lazyquery.go` — `LazyQuerier`
```go
func (l LazyQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, selectSorted bool,
    params *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    future := make(chan storage.SeriesSet, 1)
    copiedParams := copyParams(params)
    go func() {
        future <- l.next.Select(ctx, selectSorted, copiedParams, matchers...)
    }()
    return &lazySeriesSet{future: future}
}
```
**Required addition:**
```go
func (l LazyQuerier) SelectSorted(ctx context.Context,
    params *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    future := make(chan storage.SeriesSet, 1)
    copiedParams := copyParams(params)
    go func() {
        future <- l.next.SelectSorted(ctx, copiedParams, matchers...)
    }()
    return &lazySeriesSet{future: future}
}
```

#### `pkg/querier/blocks_store_queryable.go` — `blocksStoreQuerier`
```go
// Select implements storage.Querier interface.
// The bool passed is ignored because the series is always sorted.
func (q *blocksStoreQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, _ bool,
    sp *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    tenantID, err := tenant.TenantID(ctx)
    ...
    return q.selectSorted(ctx, sp, tenantID, matchers...)
}
```
Note: the comment says "the bool passed is ignored because the series is always sorted." `SelectSorted` is a natural fit here — it would simply call `q.selectSorted(...)` directly without the ignored bool.

**Required addition:**
```go
func (q *blocksStoreQuerier) SelectSorted(ctx context.Context,
    sp *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    tenantID, err := tenant.TenantID(ctx)
    if err != nil {
        return storage.ErrSeriesSet(err)
    }
    return q.selectSorted(ctx, sp, tenantID, matchers...)
}
```

#### `pkg/querier/distributor_queryable.go` — `distributorQuerier`
```go
// Select implements storage.Querier interface.
// The bool passed is ignored because the series is always sorted.
func (q *distributorQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, _ bool,
    sp *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet { ... }
```
Same pattern — the bool is already ignored. **Required addition** delegates to the same body.

#### `pkg/querier/tenantfederation/merge_queryable.go` — `mergeQuerier`
```go
func (m *mergeQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, sortSeries bool,
    hints *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet { ... }
```
**Required addition:**
```go
func (m *mergeQuerier) SelectSorted(ctx context.Context,
    hints *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    return m.Select(ctx, true, hints, matchers...)
}
```

#### `pkg/frontend/querymiddleware/sharded_queryable.go` — `shardedQuerier`
```go
// Select implements storage.Querier.
// The sorted bool is ignored because the series is always sorted.
func (q *shardedQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, _ bool,
    hints *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet { ... }
```
**Required addition:**
```go
func (q *shardedQuerier) SelectSorted(ctx context.Context,
    hints *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    return q.Select(ctx, true, hints, matchers...)
}
```

#### `pkg/querier/memory_tracking_queryable.go` — `memoryTrackingQuerier`
```go
func (q *memoryTrackingQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, sortSeries bool,
    hints *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    ...
    return series.NewMemoryTrackingSeriesSet(q.inner.Select(ctx, sortSeries, hints, matchers...), memoryTracker)
}
```
**Required addition:**
```go
func (q *memoryTrackingQuerier) SelectSorted(ctx context.Context,
    hints *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    memoryTracker, err := limiter.MemoryConsumptionTrackerFromContext(ctx)
    if err != nil {
        return storage.ErrSeriesSet(err)
    }
    ctx = limiter.ContextWithNewSeriesLabelsDeduplicator(ctx, q.metrics)
    return series.NewMemoryTrackingSeriesSet(q.inner.SelectSorted(ctx, hints, matchers...), memoryTracker)
}
```

#### `pkg/querier/querier.go` — `multiQuerier` and `chunkQuerier`
`multiQuerier.Select` (line 387) is the top-level orchestrator that fans out to all applicable sub-queriers. `chunkQuerier.Select` (line 269) wraps a `storage.Querier.Select` call. Both need `SelectSorted`.

#### `pkg/ingester/mirror_querier.go` — `mirroredChunkQuerier`
This implements `storage.ChunkQuerier` (not `storage.Querier`), so it is **not directly affected** by the `Querier` interface change. However, it wraps a `storage.ChunkQuerier` delegate and would be indirectly affected if `ChunkQuerier` were similarly extended.

#### `pkg/streamingpromql/operators/selectors/selector.go` — Caller of `Querier.Select`
At line 172:
```go
s.seriesSet = s.querier.Select(ctx, true, hints, promMatchers...)
```
This is a **call site**, not an implementor. After the change, this could be updated to call `s.querier.SelectSorted(ctx, hints, promMatchers...)` to use the new, semantically cleaner API. It is not a compile error, but it is a migration opportunity.

---

### 2.4 Internal Adapter Chain

The `storage/generic.go` file defines the internal `genericQuerier` interface (line 26–29) used by `mergeGenericQuerier`. This is a **package-private** interface and does **not** need `SelectSorted` added to it — it is not `storage.Querier`. However, `querierAdapter` (line 79) wraps a `genericQuerier` and **is** a `storage.Querier`, so it needs the new method.

---

## 3. Relevant Files

| Repo | File Path | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| **prometheus** | `storage/interface.go` | **Source of truth** — defines `Querier` interface (L122–132), `MockQuerier` (L134–153), `SelectHints` (L203–250), `SeriesSet` (L412–424). `SelectSorted` is added here. `MockQuerier.SelectSorted` stub also needed. |
| **prometheus** | `storage/noop.go` | `noopQuerier` (L23) implements `Querier` via `Select` (L30). Must add `SelectSorted` returning `NoopSeriesSet()`. |
